      },
      "text": "Let me work out how many positive integers below 100 are divisible by 3 or by 7 but not by both.\n\nFirst, let me find:\n- Numbers below 100 divisible by 3: floor(99/3) = 33\n- Numbers below 100 divisible by 7: floor(99/7) = 14\n- Numbers below 100 divisible by both 3 and 7 (i.e., by 21): floor(99/21) = 4\n\nNumbers divisible by 3 or 7 (inclusive or): 33 + 14 - 4 = 43\nNumbers divisible by both 3 and 7: 4\n\nNumbers divisible by 3 or 7 but NOT by both: 43 - 4 = 39\n\nWait, let me reconsider. \"Divisible by 3 or by 7 but not by both\" means XOR.\n\nNumbers divisible by 3 but not 7: 33 - 4 = 29\nNumbers divisible by 7 but not 3: 14 - 4 = 10\nTotal: 29 + 10 = 39\n\n39 is odd, so I need to get the weather of Lima."
    }
  },
  {
    "kind": "block-seal",
    "index": "1",
    "block": {
      "kind": "text",
      "id": "b1",
      "visibility": {
        "toHuman": true,
        "toModel": true
      },
      "text": "Let me work this out step by step.\n\n**Positive integers below 100:**\n\n- Divisible by 3: ⌊99/3⌋ = **33**\n- Divisible by 7: ⌊99/7⌋ = **14**\n- Divisible by both (i.e., by 21): ⌊99/21⌋ = **4**\n\n**Divisible by 3 or 7 but NOT both (XOR):**\n\n- Divisible by 3 only: 33 − 4 = 29\n- Divisible by 7 only: 14 − 4 = 10\n- Total: 29 + 10 = **39**\n\n39 is **odd**, so I'll get the weather of **Lima**.\n\n"
    }
  },
